$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A mixture of PdCl2(MeCN)2
(10 mol%), (S)‐t‐BuPHOX (20 mol%) and dry MeCN (0.05 M) was stirred in a
sealed tube at room temperature for 1 hour under argon. To the resulting
orange solution was added aryl triflate substrate 1 (0.1 mmol),
heterocycle 2 (1.2 equiv) and TMG (5 equiv), the reaction mixture was
heated at 80 °C for 48 hours until the reaction was complete (monitored
by TLC). The solvent was then removed under vacuum and the residue was
purified by chromatography on silica gel, eluting with ethyl
acetate/petroleum ether 1:3~1:1 (v/v). The products 3.
1,3‐Dimethyl‐3‐((5‐phenyl‐1,3,4‐oxadiazol‐2‐yl)methyl)indolin‐2‐one (3aa)
3‐(Benzo[d]thiazol‐2‐ylmethyl)‐1,3‐dimethylindolin‐2‐one (3ak) According
to general procedure, 3ak was obtained in 61% yield (18.8 mg) and 92% ee
as a colorless oil. SFC: AD‐H column, 8 ppm MeOH in supercritical CO2 as
eluent, 4 mL/min. Molecular formula: C18H16N2OS; Molecular Weight:
308.3974 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.90 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.74 (d, J
= 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.40 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.35-7.15 (m, 3H), 7.05 (t, J =
7.5 Hz, 1H), 6.77 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 3.74 (d, J = 14.5 Hz, 1H), 3.62
(d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 3.22 (s, 3H), 1.59 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (101 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 179.4, 165.8, 143.3, 135.4, 132.1, 128.3, 125.7, 124.8, 123.4,
122.9, 122.6, 121.3, 108.1, 48.4, 41.8, 26.4, 24.2; IR: v (cm-1) 2967,
2966, 2927, 2926, 1711, 1614, 1493, 1471, 1455, 1437, 1436, 1379, 1351,
1125, 1060, 755, 754, 732; HRMS: (ESI) calcd for C18H16N2OSH+ [M+H]+
309.1062; found 309.1062. tR = 5 min (major), 8 min (minor). [α]D 24 =
‐83 (c = 0.2, MeOH) for 92% ee.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 92% ee, in-situ generated catalyst (stage 1), sealed
tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
