$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(R,E,E)-4-Benzylidene-2-(3-phenyl-2-propenyl)-1,2,3,4-tetrahydro-2-naphthalenol
[(R,E,E)-13]- typical procedure for desymmetrizing Heck cyclizations: At
room temperature, a sealed tube was charged with Pd(OAc)2 (4.5 mg, 0.020
mmol, 5.0 mol%), (R)-BINAP (0.019 g, 0.030 mmol, 7.5 mol%) and K2CO3
(0.220 g, 1.59 mmol) under a static pressure of argon. A solution of
triflate (E,E)-9 (0.200 g, 0.398 mmol) and degassed dry toluene (5.5 mL)
was added and the tube was sealed. The resulting suspension was
vigorously stirred for 1 h until the formation of a red homogenous
solution except for the solid base and then heated at 60°C for 36 h. At
room temperature, a small amount of silica gel was added and after
evaporation of the solvents, the crude product on silical gel was
directly purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel
(cyclohexane/t-butyl methyl ether 9:1) giving (R,E,E)-13 (0.115 g, 82%)
as a colorless oil. The enantiomeric excess was determined by HPLC
analysis (94% ee). As determined from the 1H NMR spectra, (R,E,E)-13 was
isomerically pure.
(R,Z,Z)-4-Benzylidene-2-(3-phenyl-2-propenyl)-1,2,3,4-tetrahydro-2-naphthalenol
[(R,Z,Z)-13]: According to the procedure described for (R,E,E)-13, Heck
reaction of (Z,Z)-9 (0.090 g, 0.18 mmol) with Pd(OAc)2 (2.0 mg, 0.0089
mmol, 5.0 mol%), (R)-BINAP (8.4 mg, 0.014 mmol, 7.5 mol%) and
2,2,6,6-tertamethylpiperidine (0.12 mL, 0.10 g, 0.72 mmol) in toluene
(1.8 mL) at 100°C for 20 h afforded after purification by flash column
chromatography on silica gel (cyclohexane/t-butyl methylether 9:1)
(R,Z,Z)-13 (0.039 g, 61%) along with the 2(2E)-isomer (R,Z,E)-13 (3.7 mg,
6%) and the 4E-isomer (R,E,Z)-13 (1.8 mg, 3%) as a colorless oil. The
enantiomeric excess was determined by HPLC analysis (33% ee). R f=0.31
(cyclohexane/t-butyl methyl ether 3:1); HPLC (Daicel Chiracel AD-H,
n-heptane/ i-PrOH 9:1, flow-rate=1 mL/min, λ=295 nm): t R=8.55 (S), t
R=11.63 (R); [α]D 20=-24.9 (c=1.19, CHCl3, 19% ee); 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ=7.20 (mc, 4 H), 7.06-7.15 (m, 7 H), 6.99-7.03 (m, 2 H),
6.72-6.77 (m, 1 H), 6.58 (ddd, J=11.8, 1.8, 1.8 Hz, 1 H), 6.42 (s, 1 H),
5.87 (ddd, J=11.8, 7.3, 7.3 Hz, 1 H), 2.91 (s, 2 H), 2.63 (ddd, J=15.0,
7.4, 1.8 Hz, 1 H), 2.61 (ddd, J=15.0, 7.3, 1.8 Hz, 1 H), 2.52 (dd,
J=12.9, 1.6 Hz, 1 H), 2.46 (d, J=13.0 Hz, 1 H), 1.91 (br s, 1 H) ppm; 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ=137.9, 137.4, 136.1, 134.2, 133.5, 132.2, 129.5,
129.0, 128.8, 128.7, 128.4, 128.3, 128.3, 128.1, 126.8, 126.7, 125.0,
72.2, 47.4, 42.9, 40.1 ppm; IR (CDCl3): ν=3575, 3062, 3025, 2910, 1952,
1763, 1600, 1494, 1446, 1367, 1251, 1074 cm-1; MS (EI): m/z (%): 352 (27)
[M+]; elemental analysis calcd (%) for C26H24O: C 88.60, H 6.86; found: C
88.33, H 7.01.
