$DATUM 71-43-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: In a glovebox, the alkyl iodide (1.0 equiv),
Pd(PPh3)4 (10 mol %), 1,2, 2,6,6- pentamethylpiperidine (2.0 equiv), and
benzene (0.5 M) were combined in a sealed tube with a stir bar added.
Upon removal from the glovebox, the sealed tube was placed into an oil
bath at 110°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for 24 h, after which it
was cooled to room temperature and diluted with Et2O. The reaction
mixture was washed with 1 N HCl. The reaction was then extracted with
Et2O three times. The combined organic layers were dried (MgSO4), and
concentrated. The reaction mixture was then treated with CuCl and
dissolved in CH2Cl2 in order to remove PPh3. The product was purified by
flash column chromatography with the specified solvent system.
(E)-1-(4-(2-cyclohexylvinyl)phenyl)ethanone (23b) was synthesized from
the reaction of cyclohexyl iodide (89 μL, 0.684 mmol) and 22b (50 mg,
0.342 mmol) using Method B, except Cy2NMe (146 μL, 0.684 mmol) was used
as the amine base, the reaction was run at 130°C, and the reaction time
was 4 h. PPh3 did not need to be removed prior to purification. The
product was purified by flash column chromatography (30:1 Hex:EtOAc) to
afford 23b (58.7 mg, 0.204 mmol, 60% yield) as a tan solid. IR (thin
film, cm-1) 3429, 2922, 1573, 1602, 1266, 996.1, 808.0; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.90 (d, J= 8.4 Hz, 2 H), 7.43 (d, J= 8.4 Hz, 2 H), 6.41 - 6.32
(m, 2 H), 2.60 (s, 3 H), 2.18 (m, 1 H), 1.81 (m, 3 H), 1.71 (m, 1 H),
1.40 - 1.31 (m, 2 H), 1.27 - 1.23 (m, 3 H); 13C NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
197.5, 142.8, 140.0, 135.3, 128.7, 126.5, 125.9, 41.27, 32.69, 26.51,
26.07, 25.93; LRMS (ESI) calculated for [C16H20O+H]+ 229.16, found
229.16.
