$DATUM (E)-(3-tert-Butyl buta-1,3-dienyl) benzene (entry 2). Lithium chloride
(169.6 mg, 4.00 mmol), X-Phos (9.6 mg, 0.02 mmol), 3,3- dimethyl
but-1-en-2-yl diphenylphosphate (133.0 mg, 0.40 mmol), styrene (184 μL,
1.6 mmol), Cy2NMe (170 μL, 0.80 mmol), PdCl2(COD) (5.7 mg, 0.02 mmol)
dissolved in a 1:1 DMF-Dioxane mixture (3 mL) were reacted for 24 h at
100°C. The crude product was purified by flash chromatography on silica
gel using pentane as eluent. This afforded 45 mg of the title compound
(60% yield) as an colorless oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3CN) δ (ppm)
7.52-7.50 (m, 2H), 7.38-7.34 (m, 2H), 7.29-7.25 (m, 1H), 6.95 (d, 1H, J =
15.8 Hz), 6.85 (d, 1H, J = 15.8 Hz), 5.26 (s, 1H), 4.95 (t, 1H, J = 0.8
Hz), 1.18 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CD3CN) 157.1, 138.6, 130.4, 129.6,
129.5, 128.4, 127.4, 107.8, 36.1, 29.8. Mass confirmed by GCMS analysis.
