$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedure for Suzuki-Miyaura coupling: A flame-dried 25 mL round-bottom
flask was charged with a solution of vinyl boronate (55 mg, 0.18 mmol),
trans-2-iodoacrylate (45 mg, 0.20 mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4 (20 mg, 0.018 mmol)
in THF (5 mL) under a nitrogen atmosphere. Thalium ethoxide (100 mg, 0.4
mmol) was then added slowly over 10 min. The reaction stirred at room
temperature for 12 hours. The brown suspension was then partitioned
between ether and water, and the aqueous phase was extracted twice with
ether. The combined organic phases were dried over MgSO4, filtered and
concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by silica gel
chromatography (Hex:EtOAc 8:1) yield 30 mg, 60%, as a colorless oil.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of β,β-Disubstituted Vinyl Boronates via the
Ruthenium-Catalyzed Alder Ene Reaction of Borylated Alkynes and Alkenes
