$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: a) General procedure A: Asymmetric
alkenylative Heck reaction General Procedure: To a dry 20 ml
scintillation vial, equipped with a stir bar was added, Pd2dba3.CHCl3 (26
mg, 0.025 mmol, 5 mol %), ligand (16.5 mg, 0.06 mmol, 12 mol %), 3Å MS
(250mg, 50mg/mmol) and sealed using a rubber septum. The reaction vial
was evacuated and refilled with N2 three times. To this, 3 ml dimethyl
formamide (DMF) was added under nitrogen and the resulting mixture was
stirred for 10 min at room temperature And for another 10 min at 10 °C.
To this, a DMF solution (3 mL) of the substrate alkenol (S1-S7) (0.5
mmol) and alkenyl triflate (T1-T12) (0.5 mmol) were Added via syringe.
After that, the resulting mixture was stirred at 10 °C for 12-16 h,
unless otherwise mentioned. The mixture was diluted with ethyl acetate
(150 mL) and water (100 mL). The aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl
acetate (2 x 100 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with water
(2 x 50 mL), brine (1 x 50 mL), and dried over sodium sulfate. The
organic extracts were concentrated under reduced pressure, and the
resulting residue was purified by silica gel flash chromatography using 0
to 30% ethyl acetate in hexanes. The corresponding products. Compound 5g
was prepared according to the general procedure A, using T10 and reacting
with substrate S7 and purified using silica gel flash chromatography
using 10-30% EtOAc in hexanes, to afford product 5g, as a yellow oil, in
57% yield. TLC (25% ethylacetate in hexane). Rf= 0.17. [α]20 D=+37 o
(c=0.140, CHCl3). 1H-NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ=9.71 (s, 1 H), 7.68 (d, J=8
Hz, 1 H), 7.52 (t, J=7.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.34 (d, J=8.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.29 (t,
J=7.5 Hz, 1 H), 6.26 (s, 1 H), 3.04-3.01 (m, 1 H), 2.43 (t, J=7.5 Hz, 2
H), 1.77-1.55 (m, 6 H), 0.87 (t, J=7.25 Hz, 3 H). 13C-NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3) δ=201.9, 161.4, 159.6, 154.1, 131.9, 124.4, 124.1, 119.7, 117.8,
112.8, 43.9, 33.5, 27.6, 19.9, 11.7. IR (neat): 2934, 2874, 2359, 2342,
1719, 1604, 1562, 1448, 1394, 1183, cm-1. HRMS (M+Na)+ calcd. 281.1154,
obsvd. 281.1155.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, sealed tube used at stage 1, er 91:9, Heck reaction,
molecular sieves used, sealed tube used
