$DATUM 7560-83-0
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 14221-01-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 71-43-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: In a glovebox, the alkyl iodide (1.0 equiv),
Pd(PPh3)4 (10 mol %), 1,2, 2,6,6- pentamethylpiperidine (2.0 equiv), and
benzene (0.5 M) were combined in a sealed tube with a stir bar added.
Upon removal from the glovebox, the sealed tube was placed into an oil
bath at 110°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for 24 h, after which it
was cooled to room temperature and diluted with Et2O. The reaction
mixture was washed with 1 N HCl. The reaction was then extracted with
Et2O three times. The combined organic layers were dried (MgSO4), and
concentrated. The reaction mixture was then treated with CuCl and
dissolved in CH2Cl2 in order to remove PPh3. The product was purified by
flash column chromatography with the specified solvent system.
(E)-(2-cyclohexylvinyl)benzene (22) was synthesized from the reaction of
cyclohexyl iodide (340 μL, 2.62 mmol) and styrene (150 μL, 1.31 mmol)
(purified by vacuum transfer) using Method B, except Cy2NMe (563 μL, 2.62
mmol) was used as the amine base, the reaction was run at 130°C, and the
reaction time was 4 h. PPh3 did not need to be removed prior to
purification. The product was purified by flash column chromatography
(Hexanes) to afford 22 (135.2 mg, 0.725 mmol, 55% yield) as a clear oil.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, 2 eq. cyclohexyl iodide used, sealed
tube used, alkyl-Heck-type reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium-Catalyzed Heck-Type Reactions of Alkyl Iodides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bloome, Kayla S.; McMahen, Rebecca L.; Alexanian, Erik J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2011), 133(50), 20146-20148

