$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(R,E,E)-4-Benzylidene-2-(3-phenyl-2-propenyl)-1,2,3,4-tetrahydro-2-naphthalenol
[(R,E,E)-13]- typical procedure for desymmetrizing Heck cyclizations: At
room temperature, a sealed tube was charged with Pd(OAc)2 (4.5 mg, 0.020
mmol, 5.0 mol%), (R)-BINAP (0.019 g, 0.030 mmol, 7.5 mol%) and K2CO3
(0.220 g, 1.59 mmol) under a static pressure of argon. A solution of
triflate (E,E)-9 (0.200 g, 0.398 mmol) and degassed dry toluene (5.5 mL)
was added and the tube was sealed. The resulting suspension was
vigorously stirred for 1 h until the formation of a red homogenous
solution except for the solid base and then heated at 60°C for 36 h. At
room temperature, a small amount of silica gel was added and after
evaporation of the solvents, the crude product on silical gel was
directly purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel
(cyclohexane/t-butyl methyl ether 9:1) giving (R,E,E)-13 (0.115 g, 82%)
as a colorless oil. The enantiomeric excess was determined by HPLC
analysis (94% ee). As determined from the 1H NMR spectra, (R,E,E)-13 was
isomerically pure.
(R,E,E)-4-Benzylidene-2-(3-phenyl-2-propenyl)-2-triethylsilyloxy-1,2,3,4-tetrahydronaphthalene
[(R,E,E)-14]: In analogy to the procedure described for (R,E,E)-13, Heck
reaction of (E,E)-10 (0.049 g, 0.079 mmol) with Pd(OAc)2 (0.89 mg, 0.0039
mmol, 5.0 mol%), (R)-BINAP (3.7 mg, 0.0059 mmol, 7.5 mol%) and K2CO3
(0.044 g, 0.32 mmol) in toluene (0.79 mL) at 80°C for 15 h provided after
purification by flash column chromatography on silica gel
(cyclohexane/t-butyl methyl ether 95:5) (R,E,E)-14 (0.020 g, 55%) as a
colorless oil. The enantiomeric excess was determined by HPLC analysis
(2% ee). As determined from the 1H NMR spectra, (R,E,E)-14 was
isomerically pure. R f=0.83 (cyclohexane/t-butyl methyl ether 9:1); HPLC
(Daicel Chiracel AD, n-heptane/i-PrOH 100:1, flowrate= 0.5 mL/min, λ=295
nm): t R=10.38 min (S), t R=13.04 min (R); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3):
δ=7.73-7.77 (m, 1 H), 7.29-7.37 (m, 4 H), 7.08-7.25 (m, 10 H), 6.20 (d,
J=15.9 Hz, 1 H), 6.13 (ddd, J=15.8, 6.5, 6.5 Hz, 1 H), 3.07 (dd, J=14.1,
0.9 Hz, 1H), 3.02 (s, 2 H), 2.79 (dd, J=13.9, 2.1 Hz, 1 H ), 2.32 (mc, 2
H), 0.89 (t, J=7.9 Hz, 9 H), 0.55 (q, J=7.9 Hz, 6 H) ppm; 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ=138.0, 137.8, 135.8, 135.6, 135.2, 132.9, 129.8, 129.4,
128.4, 128.2, 127.8, 126.8, 126.7, 126.4, 126.3, 126.0, 125.6, 123.9,
75.1, 43.8, 43.6, 40.5, 7.2, 6.9 ppm; IR (CHCl3): ν=3688, 3026, 2959,
2878, 1772, 1699, 1652, 1521, 1421, 1232, 1109, 1016, 929 cm-1; MS (EI):
m/z (%): 349 (79) [(M-C9H9)+]; HRMS (EI): m/z calcd for C23H29OSi
[(M-C9H9)+]: 349.19932; found: 349.19877.
