$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A mixture of PdCl2(MeCN)2
(10 mol%), (S)‐t‐BuPHOX (20 mol%) and dry MeCN (0.05 M) was stirred in a
sealed tube at room temperature for 1 hour under argon. To the resulting
orange solution was added aryl triflate substrate 1 (0.1 mmol),
heterocycle 2 (1.2 equiv) and TMG (5 equiv), the reaction mixture was
heated at 80 °C for 48 hours until the reaction was complete (monitored
by TLC). The solvent was then removed under vacuum and the residue was
purified by chromatography on silica gel, eluting with ethyl
acetate/petroleum ether 1:3~1:1 (v/v). The products 3.
1,3‐Dimethyl‐3‐((5‐phenyl‐1,3,4‐oxadiazol‐2‐yl)methyl)indolin‐2‐one (3aa)
6‐Chloro‐1,3‐dimethyl‐3‐((5‐phenyl‐1,3,4‐oxadiazol‐2‐yl)methyl)indolin‐2‐one
(3qd) According to general procedure, 3qd was obtained in 55% yield (19.5
mg) and 82% ee as a colorless oil. SFC: AD‐H column, 10 ppm MeOH in
supercritical CO2 as eluent, 4 mL/min. Molecular formula: C19H16ClN3O2;
Molecular Weight: 353.8022 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.90 (d, J = 7.0
Hz, 2H), 7.64‐7.38 (m, 3H), 7.12 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.01 (d, J = 7.9
Hz, 1H), 6.81 (s, 1H), 3.44 (d, J = 15.5 Hz, 1H), 3.39 (d, J = 15.4 Hz,
1H), 3.23 (s, 3H), 1.55 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ 178.8,
164.8, 162.9, 144.2, 134.5, 131.8, 130.0, 129.1, 126.7, 124.1, 123.7,
122.6, 109.2, 46.5, 33.2, 26.6, 23.6; IR: v (cm-1) 2970, 2929, 1716,
1609, 1495, 1371, 1292, 1240, 1028, 812, 731; HRMS: (ESI) calcd for
C19H16N3OCl35Na+ [M+Na]+ 376.0829; found 376.0829; C19H16N3OCl37Na+
[M+Na]+ 378.0799; found 378.0806. tR = 7 min (major), 10 min (minor) [α]D
28 = 107 (c = 0.4, CHCl3) for 83% ee.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 82% ee, in-situ generated catalyst (stage 1), sealed
tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
