$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Diastereoselective Heck-type Styrylation of
22a to Yield trans-23a (eq 12) Anhydrous cobalt(II) chloride (22 mg, 0.17
mmol) and DPPH (91 mg, 0.20 mmol) were mixed in diethyl ether (10 mL) at
room temperature for 45 min under argon. The bromide 22a (300 mg, 1.68
mmol) in diethyl ether (2 mL), p-methoxystyrene (226 mg, 1.68 mmol), and
trimethylsilylmethylmagnesium chloride (2 M in diethyl ether, 2.5 mL, 5.0
mmol) were sequentially added dropwise to the [CoCl2(dpph)] complex. The
mixture formed was then heated under reflux overnight. The product was
extracted with diethyl ether (3 × 10 mL). The combined organic extracts
were dried and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel, using 5% Et2O in hexane as eluent, to
furnish 23a (218 mg, 0.94 mmol, 56%). The product 23a was a mixture of
two diastereoisomers (trans/cis = 88:12), judging from the 1H NMR signals
of their protons at the methoxy-substituted carbons. The mixture was
partly separated by column chromatography with a solvent gradient ranging
from 2 to 10% Et2O in hexane to provide trans-23a (111 mg, 0.48 mmol,
28%). No attempts were made to isolate cis-23a.
2-Methoxy-3-[(E)-2-(p-methoxyphenyl)ethenyl]-1-oxacyclopentane (23b)
trans-23b: IR (neat) 2895, 1607, 1252, 1036 cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz)
δ 1.79 (m, 1H), 2.26 (m, 1H), 2.91 (q, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 3.36 (s, 3H),
3.80 (s, 3H), 3.97 (q, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 4.03 (td, J = 8.0. 5.5 Hz, 1H),
4.81 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 5.99 (dd, J = 16.0, 9.0 Hz, 1H), 6.42 (d, J =
16.0 Hz, 1H), 6.82-6.85 (m, 2H), 7.26-7.29 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125.6
MHz) δ 31.5, 49.2, 55.2, 55.5, 67.1, 109.6, 114.1, 127.5, 127.6, 130.0,
130.4, 159.2; Found: C, 71.52, H, 7.76%. Calcd for C14H18O3: C, 71.77, H,
7.74%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, trans:cis 91:9, mixture of isomers
