$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative procedure for the Alder ene
reaction: To a solution of borylated alkyne (21 mg, 0.12 mmol) and alkene
(14 mg, 0.10 mmol) in acetone (0.2 mL) under a nitrogen atmosphere was
added RuCp(CH3CN)3PF6 (4 mg, 0.010 mmol). The reaction was stirred at
room temperature for approximately 2 hours, after which time the solvent
was removed in vacuo and the residue was purified by silica gel
chromatography (hexane:ether 5:1). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.73 (dt, J
= 15.3, 6.8 Hz, 1H), 5.55 (dd, J = 15.3, 6.8 Hz, 1H), 5.16 (s, 1H), 5.15
(p, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 4.16 (q, J = 7.0 Hz, 2H), 3.12 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H),
1.82 (s, 3H), 1.34 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H), 1.29 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 1.24
(s, 12H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 160.35, 154.66, 132.10, 130.40,
82.83, 75.19, 63.79, 39.24, 26.47, 24.98, 20.55, 14.43; HRMS (ESI) calcd
for C17H29BO5 [M+Na]+: 347.2066, found 347.2075.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, 9:1 mixt. of cis:trans isomers, isomers
not sepd.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
