$DATUM 71-43-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: In a glovebox, the alkyl iodide (1.0 equiv),
Pd(PPh3)4 (10 mol %), 1,2, 2,6,6- pentamethylpiperidine (2.0 equiv), and
benzene (0.5 M) were combined in a sealed tube with a stir bar added.
Upon removal from the glovebox, the sealed tube was placed into an oil
bath at 110°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for 24 h, after which it
was cooled to room temperature and diluted with Et2O. The reaction
mixture was washed with 1 N HCl. The reaction was then extracted with
Et2O three times. The combined organic layers were dried (MgSO4), and
concentrated. The reaction mixture was then treated with CuCl and
dissolved in CH2Cl2 in order to remove PPh3. The product was purified by
flash column chromatography with the specified solvent system.
(E)-(4-(2-cyclohexylvinyl)phenyl)methanol (23c) was synthesized from the
reaction of cyclohexyl iodide (97 μL, 0.745 mmol) and 22c (50 mg, 0.372
mmol) using Method B, except Cy2NMe (160 μL, 0.745 mmol) was used as the
amine base, the reaction was run at 130°C, and the reaction time was 4 h.
PPh3 did not need to be removed prior to purification. The product was
purified by flash column chromatography (4:1 Hex:EtOAc) to afford 23b
(41.0 mg, 0.190 mmol, 51% yield) as a white solid. IR (thin film, cm-1)
3400, 1650, 1447, 1265, 966.1, 738.6; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.36 (d,
J= 7.8 Hz, 2 H), 7.30 (d, J= 8.4 Hz, 2 H), 6.36 (d, J= 16.2 Hz, 1 H),
6.20 (dd, J= 10.4 Hz, J= 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 4.68 (s, 2 H), 2.15 (m, 1 H), 2.14
(m, 1 H), 1.79 (m, 4 H), 1.70 (m, 1 H), 1.37 - 1.30 (m, 2 H), 1.25 - 1.16
(m, 3 H); 13C NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 139.3, 137.6, 137.0, 127.2, 126.8,
126.1, 65.17, 41.12, 32.91, 26.14, 26.01; LRMS (ESI) calculated for
[C15H20O+Na]+ 239.14, found 239.16.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, 2 eq. cyclohexyl iodide used, sealed
tube used, alkyl-Heck-type reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium-Catalyzed Heck-Type Reactions of Alkyl Iodides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
