$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: ii) Procedures for the synthesis of product 2.
0.3 mmol (1 equiv) of N-vinylacetamide 1, 0.03 mmol (10 mol%, 6.8 mg)
palladium (II)acetate and 0.06 mmol (20 mol%, 15.8 mg) of
triphenylphosphine were dissolved in 5 mL of DMF in a screw cap vial
under argon atmosphere. Then 0.6 mmol (60.7 mg, 2.0 equiv) triethylamine
was added to the solution and the vial was heated at 120 °C till the
starting material consumed completely. The solution was cooled to room
temperature and diluted with ethyl acetate, washed with saturated
ammonium chloride solution and brine. The organic layer was dried with
anhydrous NaSO4 and filtered. The final filtrate was concentrated under
vacuum to afford the crude product which was isolated through flash
column chromatography (Eluent: petrol ether/ethyl acetate) to furnish the
related product 2. N-(2-(1-(benzofuran-2-yl)vinyl)benzyl)acetamide 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.39 (dd, J = 8.2, 0.7 Hz, 1H), 7.34 (d, J = 7.6 Hz,
2H), 7.33-7.24 (m, 2H), 7.22-7.18 (m, 3H), 7.12-7.04 (m, 1H), 6.11 (d, J
= 1.1 Hz, 1H), 6.10 (s, 1H), 5.66 (s, 1H), 5.20 (d, J = 1.1 Hz, 1H), 4.30
(d, J = 5.8 Hz, 2H), 1.74 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 169.79,
155.93, 155.09, 138.21, 137.51, 136.52, 130.17, 128.97, 128.70, 128.69,
127.53, 125.13, 123.00, 121.19, 115.90, 111.13, 105.90, 41.38, 23.08.
