$DATUM General Procedure for Heck Arylation of 1 and Subsequent Hydrolysis
Producing 4. The reactants were added to a reaction vial in the following
order: aryl iodide 2 (0.60 mmol), enol ether 1 (0.78 mmol, 0.132 g),
Pd(OAc)2 (0.018 mmol, 0.004 g), NaOAc (0.72 mmol, 0.059 g), LiCl (1.20
mmol, 0.051 g), K2CO3 (0.72 mmol, 0.100 g), DMF (2 mL) and water (0.2
mL). The tube was closed and the contents were magnetically stirred and
heated for 1-7 days (2a 42 h, 70 °C, 2c 72 h, 80 °C, 2e 42 h, 70 °C). The
reaction was interrupted when GC-MS analysis showed complete conversion.
After cooling, 0.5 mL concd HCl was added and the contents stirred for 30
min. After complete hydrolysis of 3 (GC-MS) the reaction mixture was
diluted with 10 mL 0.5 M HCl and extracted five times with diethyl ether.
The ethereal phases were washed twice with 0.1 M NaOH and dried with
K2CO3(s). Evaporation of the solvent and silica column chromatography
afforded pure products.
(rac)-2-(2-Methoxy-phenyl)-2-methyl-cyclopentanone (4a) 2 Compound 4a was
obtained in 49% yield after silica column chromatography (hexane-diethyl
ether, 70:30).
