$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of
{4-[1-(R)-Methyl-2-(1-methyl-pyrrolidin-2-(S)-ylmethoxy)-cyclopent-2-enyl]-phenyl}-phenyl-methanone
(7g). The reactants were added to the reaction vial in the following
order: 4-iodobenzophenone 2h (0.60 mmol, 0.185 g), enol ether 6a (0.78
mmol, 0.152 g), Pd(OAc)2 (0.018 mmol, 0.004 g), NaOAc (0.72 mmol, 0.059
g), LiCl (1.20 mmol, 0.051 g), K2CO3 (0.72 mmol, 0.100 g), DMF (2 mL) and
water (0.2 mL). The vial was closed and the contents were magnetically
stirred and heated for 24 h. After cooling, the reaction mixture was
diluted with diethyl ether and was washed five times with NaOH (0.1 M).
The combined aqueous phases were additionally extracted twice with
diethyl ether. The ethereal phases were combined and dried with K2CO3
(s). Evaporation of the solvent and silica column chromatography
(hexane/diethyl ether/triethylamine, 1:1:0.05) yielded 0.119 g pure
product 7g (53%). (R)-2-(4-Benzoyl-phenyl)-2-methyl-cyclopentanone (4g)
The enol ether 7g (0.032 g) was carefully placed in a vial together with
1 mL concentrated HCl and 3 mL diethyl ether. The vial was closed and
stirred at room temperature over night. The ether layer was separated and
the acidic aqueous layer extracted three times with diethyl ether. The
organic phases were combined and dried with K2CO3 (s). Evaporation of the
solvent furnished 0.021 g pure product 4g (88%) in 97% ee. [α] D 23 =
+48°
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, KEY STEP, enantioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A new highly asymmetric chelation-controlled Heck arylation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Nilsson, Peter; Larhed, Mats; Hallberg, Anders
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2003), 125(12), 3430-3431

