$DATUM rac-1-(cis-1H-Carbazol-9(2H,4aH,9aH)-yl)ethanone (33): In a sealable
pressure tube were placed a stir bar, 26c (0.200 g, 0.500 mmol, 3:2
anti:syn), Pd2(dba)3.CHCl3 (0.026 g, 0.025 mmol), and P(o-tol)3 (0.040 g,
0.132 mmol). A degassed 10:1 MeCN:H2O solvent mixture (6 mL) was added,
followed by Me2NBu (0.121 g, 1.20 mmol). The tube was sealed, heated at
80 °C for 6 h, and recooled to room temperature. Saturated aqueous NH4Cl
(10 mL) was added, and the mixture was extracted with EtOAc (3 x 10 mL).
The combined organic layers were washed with brine (1 x 10 mL), dried
over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated by rotary evaporation. Column
chromatography (2 columns, 1:3 pentane:Et2O) provided the title compound
(0.061 g, 47%) as a yellow oil in a 3:1 ratio of amide rotamers. 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.14 (br d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H, major), 7.19 (t, J = 7.5
Hz, 2H, both), 7.17 (br m, minor), 7.05 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H, both),
6.17-6.02 (br m, 1H, both), 6.00-5.90 (m, 1H, both), 4.88 (br s, 1H,
minor), 4.39 (m, 1H, major), 3.94 (br s, 1H, major), 3.80 (br s, 1H,
minor), 2.41 (s, 3H, minor), 2.31 (s, 3H, major), 2.21-1.91 (m, 3H,
both), 1.63-1.45 (m, 1H, major), 1.38-1.20 (br m, 1H, minor); 13C NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.9, 140.7, 128.1, 127.4, 123.9 (2C, accidental
isochrony), 123.2, 118.1, 60.4, 40.6, 25.0, 23.2, 22.8, peaks from the
minor rotamer were also seen at 129.0, 124.5, 115.3, 59.6, 39.2, 24.2;
FTIR (neat, cm-1) 3031, 2935, 2841, 1650, 1480, 1403, 1319, 1080, 1015,
912, 730; LRMS (EI) m/z 213 (M+, 60), 171 (72), 170 (55), 156 (52), 143
(42), 130 (100), 77 (30); HRMS (EI) calcd for C14H15NO [M]+: 213.1154,
found: 213.1153.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Heck reaction, sealed tube used
