$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Experimental Procedure of the
Asymmetric Heck Reaction. Pd(dba)2 (8.6 mg, 0.015 mmol), ligand (0.03
mmol), and solvent (2.5 mL) were placed under an argon atmosphere in a
Schlenk tube with a magnetic stirring bar. After the mixture stirred for
30 min, phenyl triflate (112 mg, 0.5 mmol) was added, followed by the
addition of 2,3-dihydrofuran (0.15 mL, 2 mmol) and i-Pr2NEt (0.17 mL, 1
mmol). The mixture was stirred at 60 °C for about 20 h until the reaction
was completed monitored by TLC. The reaction mixture was quenched with
additional EtOAc (2 mL), and the resulting suspension was filtered
through a short silica gel column to removed the palladium black. The
solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the mixture was purified
by flash chromatography on silica gel to afford a mixture of 13 and 14 as
a colorless oil.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Heck reaction, in-situ generated catalyst, product
depends on phosphine ligand used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Dramatic Switch of Enantioselectivity in Asymmetric Heck Reaction by
Benzylic Substituents of Ligands
